        <body>
            <div xml:id="d63">

                <pb facs="0216" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v09/pg186"/>

                <head>63. Memorandum From the Deputy Under Secretary of State for Economic Affairs
                    (Prochnow) to the Under Secretary of State (Hoover)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d63-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>OTC Legislation</item>
                </list>
                <p>As you know, Mr. John Leddy has charge in the E Area of handling all OTC matters.
                    Mr. Leddy prepared a comprehensive and thorough program for the advancement of
                    this legislation and has pursued it aggressively. There have been many comments
                    that the presentation by the Administration has been exceptionally good. We <pb
                        facs="0217" n="187" xml:id="pg187"/> are getting strong press support. We
                    expect to continue in the weeks ahead to seek every means of advancing the
                    legislation.</p>
                <p>The E Staff has also analyzed the question of what course to pursue if it became
                    a serious question of whether the legislation would pass. The analysis of the E
                    Staff, as well as the position recommended by the Staff, is found in the
                    attached memorandum from Mr. Thibodeaux.</p>


                <xi:include href="d63-a1.xml" xpointer="d63-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
